{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1221354-where-to-start","id":1221354,"title":"Where to start ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-22T19:39:20-07:00","id":1221354,"title":"Where to start ?","content":"Hello, im Crowley.<br /> <br /> i been running MtAs for a while now but im quite curious about awakening. I have the first edition and only recently i was able to get ahold of second edition..so..which books are a must read when it comes to awakening? any general tips or advices for someone more familiar with ascension?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T19:45:40-07:00","id":1221356,"title":"","content":"Well the only published 2E materials are the core, Dark Eras and Dark Eras Companion IIRC. Reading stuff in that order sounds nice. <br /> <br /> Among 1E books, the developer himself recommended Astral Realms, Left-Handed Path, and a bunch I don\u2019t remember at the top of my head. I\u2019d personally throw in the six Order \u201csplat book\u201d as well. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> From an Ascension background... first, magic doesn\u2019t come from belief. Your cultural upbringing and worldview informs you how you interpret what you see and what you decide to do as a mage, thus indirectly shaping your magic, but it is never a source of your magic. Objective truth, subjective interpretations. <br /> <br /> Related to this, the Diamond Orders aren\u2019t imposing an \u201cAtlantean dogma\u201d like the Traditions are doing with the nine Spheres model. This may seem unrelated and out of the blue at the moment, but a LOT of recent debates and discussions here in the Awakening forums ultimately stem from this.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: See also the thread named \u201cGreat Cults of Major Religions,\u201d at the moment right below this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 05-22-2018, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T01:58:57-07:00","id":1221420,"title":"","content":"Honestly, all you need is the core book. If you want to incorporate 1e things, you can absolutely look to those books, but nothing says you have to. Personally, I don't include 1e books as required reading because I'm not interested in forcing my players to go back an edition to play the current edition.<br /> <br /> I'm afraid I'm not super familiar with ascension (only ever played one game) but Hermit has it right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T11:43:02-07:00","id":1221779,"title":"","content":"I'd also recommend Intruders, the Abyss book. It's pretty useful for off the wall antagonists. I think that Mage the Awakening has a more occult feel to it than Ascension does. It's about discovering Truth and solving Mysteries, more than paradigms of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T09:52:05-07:00","id":1224729,"title":"","content":"Lets see, there are plenty of great resources. Both Mage games are incredible, but have different feels to them. So here is what I will do, I will list generally good resources for the many focuses your campaign can have, then you can pick the ones best suited to your players. If any topic is missing, let me know and I will fine tune my suggestions.<br /> <br /> The 2ed book is very good point to start, Tome of the Mysteries for a lot of cool ways to use magic, Invaders:Encounters with the Abyss has some excellent plot hooks, Book of Spirits fleshes out the Shadow very well, Astral Realms for trips to the collective unconcious, Book of the Dead (a Geist book) for the Underworld, Imperial Mysteries if you want to make grand chessmaster archmage NPCs and Secrets of the Ruined Temple if you want a more Indiana Jones globetrotting campaign.<br /> <br /> From these forums, I cannot recommend Dave's APs enough, they are fantastic, you can find an index here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/31354-dave-s-actual-play-thread-can-someone-give-me-the-links\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/31354-dave-s-actual-play-thread-can-someone-give-me-the-links\"> Dave's Actual Play Thread, can someone give me the links? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/31354-dave-s-actual-play-thread-can-someone-give-me-the-links\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/31354-dave-s-actual-play-thread-can-someone-give-me-the-links </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Hey can I get the link to Dave's Actual Play threads that seem to get nothing but outstanding reviews? It was Broken Diamond right? Or were there multiple ones? Can someone post the Links? </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If you want a condensed version, try reading Bleak House (a one shot) and his initial notes on Broken Diamond, they are tremendously helpful for getting the feel of the setting. I recommend them in general, apart from being very entertaining, his and the player's notes are a master class on storytelling and GMing, while being clear and concise. There is also these descriptions of Active Mage Sight that give a cool glimpse on how mages see the world through the lens of their Path (the links are in the last post of the page):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/72127-describing-the-effects-of-mage-sight\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/72127-describing-the-effects-of-mage-sight\"> Describing the Effects of Mage Sight - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/72127-describing-the-effects-of-mage-sight\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/72127-describing-the-effects-of-mage-sight </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I'm having a really rough time figuring out how to describe what my players see when they use Mage Sight. I understand the mechanics of it but not the visuals. I found a few examples in the core book under Resonance (Life is scent and taste, Forces is sound) but that unfortunately didn't get me very far. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I also recommend the 1001 Mage story hooks for ideas to start the campaign:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/11947-1001-mage-story-hooks\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/11947-1001-mage-story-hooks\"> 1001 Mage Story Hooks - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/11947-1001-mage-story-hooks\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/11947-1001-mage-story-hooks </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Reposting my old 1001 Mage Story Hooks thread here, because that sort of thread tends to be useful. Please be aware that the numbers won't be consecutive - I </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As for spirits (which are delved more in-depth in Werewolf: The Forsaken), I suggest The Angel of Pain: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/794977-spirit-rite-the-pain-angel\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/794977-spirit-rite-the-pain-angel\"> Spirit &amp; Rite: The Pain Angel - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/794977-spirit-rite-the-pain-angel\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/794977-spirit-rite-the-pain-angel </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Something unpleasant from one of my games that I felt the urge to write up and throw onto the forum. The Pain Angel The hospital&rsquo;s car park is a wasteland in the Shadow. It is a great expanse of cracked, broken, scoured asphalt and concrete that stretches across a vast distance to the looming structure at its heart. Lumpen, rusting hulks of ruined vehicles slump and die in its merciless grasp. Occasional trees, gnarled and twisted, writhe up from sundered earth towards the fulminating sky of the Hisil. Tall, tottering shapes move through the gloom on streetlamp legs of metal and plastic, their </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> and Five Pounds of Meat:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1176040-five-pounds-of-meat/page4\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1176040-five-pounds-of-meat/page4\"> Five Pounds Of Meat - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1176040-five-pounds-of-meat/page4\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1176040-five-pounds-of-meat/page4 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Alright, let's do this. Let me crack open a can of nightmare fuel to buoy me along through it. Time to vote on meaty, fleshy things. Do you want: \u200ba) Five nasty, fleshy things that werewolves suffer or can do to themselves - might be diseases, crippling weird injuries, profane consumptions, body modifications, that sort of thing; or \u200bb) Five types of nasty antagonist with all sorts of body-horror to them - might be cults of flesh, contaminating horrors, or other violations of the laws of bone and sinew. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They are both by the WtF dev and are bone chillingly great. Not only do they help you grasp the feel of the Shadow and how to build a powerful spirit, they also sell you on why even a master of Spirit will be absolutely TERRIFIED at the mere suggestion of going to the Shadow, threading ever so carefully.<br /> <br /> Lastly, if you want a more lighthearted campaign, I suggets The Voice of Freedom:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?408237-Mage-the-Awakening-The-Voice-of-Freedom\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...ice-of-Freedom</a><br /> <br /> That is all that comes to mind right now, hope it is useful to you. Welcome to Mage: The Awakening, hope you have a blast <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T14:25:34-07:00","id":1233508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1221354-where-to-start?p=1221779#post1221779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also recommend Intruders, the Abyss book. It's pretty useful for off the wall antagonists. I think that Mage the Awakening has a more occult feel to it than Ascension does. It's about discovering Truth and solving Mysteries, more than paradigms of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Intruders: Encounters with the Abyss is amazing. The diversity of potential antagonists is really amazing. Makes you think about Abyssal entities in a way you wouldn't expect. For example one of them shows up as a screwdriver, or pocket calculator, or some other small useful tool that helps it's wielder creative impossible inventions, while another is a pathway that if you walk along it you get consumed by the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T02:05:00-07:00","id":1234563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TenguGrib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1221354-where-to-start?p=1233508#post1233508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Intruders: Encounters with the Abyss is amazing. The diversity of potential antagonists is really amazing. Makes you think about Abyssal entities in a way you wouldn't expect. For example one of them shows up as a screwdriver, or pocket calculator, or some other small useful tool that helps it's wielder creative impossible inventions, while another is a pathway that if you walk along it you get consumed by the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>my favorite is math-man-lex-luthor. anumeris is just delightful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}